<title>USA: Pancho's says to take Q2 charge.</title>
<headline>Pancho's says to take Q2 charge.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pancho's Mexican Buffet Inc said Tuesday it closed seven stores, and will end its participation in the Guadalajara, Mexico operation.</p>
<p>The company said these moves are part of a restructuring plan formed for the second fiscal quarter ended March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>The company said a charge to earnings of between $4 million and $5 million, as a result of these steps, will be recorded in its second fiscal quarter. Second quarter results will be reported later this month.</p>
</text>
